---
/**
 * HomepageHero — homepage hero (homepage-specific component).
 *
 * CLEAN-SLATE BUILD. This is a from-authority-only implementation of the locked
 * hero contract. It does not reuse, refactor, or inherit markup, CSS, class
 * names, spacing, typography, overlay, image crop, or layout from the rejected
 * legacy HomeHero.astro (deleted). Every decision below is derived from the
 * current approved design authority:
 *
 *   Contract:  docs/home/home-components/03-home-hero.md (exact V1 spec)
 *   Blueprint: docs/home/reference/blueprint.md §7 (Hero)
 *   Tokens:    docs/home/home-components/00-token-matrix.md
 *   Theme:     Theme V2 (Platinum) — generated/theme.css (active)
 *
 * Identity (blueprint §7, refined): a FULL-BLEED NEAR-VIEWPORT PHOTOGRAPHIC
 * HERO. The Mercedes S-Class photograph fills the entire section edge to edge
 * across the full page width; the sticky SiteHeader overlays it at the page
 * top (the page pulls the hero up under the header via --site-header-height;
 * the header's z-index keeps it above the media). A controlled directional
 * overlay (semantic dark tokens via color-mix — no raw rgba, no gold, no glow)
 * protects overlaid text — stronger behind the left copy, a darkened top strip
 * for header-chrome legibility, a bottom settle for the CTAs — while keeping
 * the car the focal subject. It is NOT a contained rounded card/panel, NOT a
 * centered template, NOT a split with a separate image column — the image is
 * the canvas.
 *
 * Composition: the <section> IS the media canvas (full-bleed, no radius). ONE
 * PageContainer lives inside it for CONTENT alignment only — the copy grid is
 * container-capped + page-guttered, the media is not. Desktop 7/5 content
 * placement (left copy / right support statement) is CONTENT-PLACEMENT only —
 * it never creates a separate visual image container (blueprint §7 /
 * blueprint-to-ui §18). Mobile/tablet collapse to a single reading column.
 *
 * Height: near-viewport min-block-size (svh with a vh fallback), content-safe
 * — there is NO max-block-size / aspect-ratio, so the hero grows when H1/CTA
 * copy wraps to more lines instead of clipping the action row. It is not a
 * forced 100vh for spectacle; it just occupies most of the opening viewport.
 *
 * H1 (03 §Typography / task §6 / task §8): the page's single <h1>, left-aligned,
 * on the active Theme V2 heading font (Inter Tight via --font-heading — a
 * variable face covering the full weight range). The H1 renders at the semantic
 * --font-weight-regular (400); the explicit weight overrides the UA bold default
 * — a controlled regular, not heavy/bold (task §8: avoid newspaper ultra-light
 * and marketing extra-bold extremes). Semantic h1 role (--text-h1), NOT
 * display-scale — controlled, wraps naturally, never theatrical.
 *
 * CTA hierarchy (03 §Colors / DESIGN.md §8): primary Book → <Link variant="cta">
 * (platinum fill + on-light text); secondary → <Link variant="button"> (outlined).
 * The foundation <Link> owns routing (getPath — FND-I18N-03), focus-visible,
 * 44×44 targets, and prefetch — no hero-specific button variant, no local .cta
 * classes, no client JS.
 *
 * Right-side support (blueprint §7 / 03 §Desktop): a small, restrained,
 * operational text block with a subtle divider — not cards, stats, badges, or
 * icons. Optional only because the editorial hero block does not author it yet
 * (blueprint §20); when supplied, the 7/5 split activates.
 *
 * Image / LCP (03 §Surface/image / responsive-images-performance): the hero
 * image is the page LCP, so astro:assets <Image> is used directly (the
 * foundation Image primitive types `src: string` and can't accept an imported
 * ImageMetadata — FND-IMG-08 only bans raw <img>/<picture>) with eager loading
 * + fetchpriority="high" + responsive widths/sizes at 100vw (full-bleed). It is
 * decorative atmosphere behind the H1/copy (alt="" + role="presentation") — the
 * title carries the meaning, never copied into alt (imagery-art-direction §19).
 *
 * Motion (task §24): STATIC. No entrance animation, no background zoom/pan,
 * no parallax, no IntersectionObserver. The hero is a still composition; the
 * only transitions are the <Link> hover/focus color shifts already owned by the
 * primitive. (Task §24 is stricter than 03 §Motion's permissive language; the
 * stricter, explicit instruction wins.)
 *
 * Breakpoints (task §21 / task 1D): the 7/5 desktop split activates at xl
 * (80rem / 1280px), NOT lg — at 1024–1279px the copy would be too cramped for
 * a side-by-side support column, so laptop stays a comfortable full-width
 * single column. The support statement follows below the CTA group below xl.
 * (Task §21 overrides 03 §Mobile's 48rem split point for the hero; task 1D
 * pushes the split from lg to xl on evidence that lg is too early.) Mobile/
 * tablet (<80rem): single reading column, content-driven height.
 *
 * CSS: scoped <style> with var() tokens only (the correct home for complex
 * art-direction — tailwind-v4 §scoped-styles). Logical properties only
 * (FND-I18N-13). class passthrough is layout-only (FND-UI-06). No raw hex,
 * no raw rgba, no brand-font literals (FND-THEME-09 / task §31).
 *
 * NOTE: the hero-under-header offset (margin-block-start: -1*var(--site-header-
 * height)) is owned by the homepage PAGE, not this component — the component is
 * reused in /dev/ui where the hero is not the first element under a header.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import PageContainer from "../../foundation/ui/PageContainer.astro";
import Link from "../../foundation/ui/Link.astro";
import type { HomepageHeroProps } from "./HomepageHero.types.ts";

type Props = HomepageHeroProps;

const {
  title,
  description,
  primaryAction,
  secondaryAction,
  supportText,
  image,
  imageAlt = "",
  locale,
  class: className,
} = Astro.props;

const titleId = "homepage-hero-title";
const hasSupport = Boolean(supportText);
// Alt contract: empty alt = decorative atmosphere (alt="" + role="presentation")
// — the H1 carries the meaning. Non-empty = informative image with that alt.
// The title is never copied into alt (imagery-art-direction §19; task §25).
const isDecorative = imageAlt === "";
---

<section class:list={["homepage-hero", className]} aria-labelledby={titleId}>
  {/* Full-bleed S-Class background (blueprint §7). The section IS the media
      canvas — no contained panel, no radius, full page width behind the
      overlaid sticky SiteHeader. Decorative atmosphere behind the H1/copy but
      the page LCP — so eager + fetchpriority="high" + responsive widths at
      100vw. object-cover; object-position biases the subject right so the left
      copy keeps negative space (asset-specific crop, reviewed per breakpoint
      — task §13). */}
  <Image
    class="homepage-hero__image"
    src={image}
    alt={imageAlt}
    role={isDecorative ? "presentation" : undefined}
    loading="eager"
    fetchpriority="high"
    widths={[640, 768, 1024, 1536, 1920]}
    sizes="100vw"
  />

  {/* Controlled directional overlay (03 §Surface/image), rebuilt for the
      full-width canvas. Stronger behind the left copy, a darkened top strip so
      the overlaid Header chrome (logo / nav / Book / language) keeps AA
      contrast over the photograph, and a bottom settle so the CTAs + support
      keep AA contrast at every crop. Built ONLY from --color-background via
      color-mix (the repo scrim convention — no raw rgba, no gold, no glow).
      Decorative (aria-hidden). */}
  <div class="homepage-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {/* Content shell — a raw HomepageHero-owned <div>, NOT a class forwarded onto
     PageContainer's root. Astro does not propagate a parent component's scope id
     onto a child component's root element, so a scoped rule on a class forwarded
     to PageContainer→Container would compile with this component's cid but never
     match the rendered node (AGENTS.md §7; DESIGN.md §15). Keeping
     homepage-hero__inner on a div this component renders directly makes the
     scoped z-index:2 + block-padding rule match, so the content stacks above
     the image/scrim. PageContainer inside caps content to --container-main +
     owns the page gutter (full-bleed outer media + contained inner content —
     01-system-rules §1). The section grid grounds this cell toward the lower /
     optical region (align-items: end — blueprint §7). Generous block-end
     padding keeps the <Link> focus ring (outline 2px + offset 2px) clear of the
     section edge (WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.11 — ServiceCard pattern). */}
  <div class="homepage-hero__inner">
    <PageContainer>
      <div
        class:list={[
          "homepage-hero__content",
          hasSupport && "homepage-hero__content--split",
        ]}
      >
        <div class="homepage-hero__copy">
          <h1 id={titleId} class="homepage-hero__title">{title}</h1>
          {description ? (
            <p class="homepage-hero__desc">{description}</p>
          ) : null}

          <div class="homepage-hero__actions">
            <Link
              variant="cta"
              to={primaryAction.to}
              href={primaryAction.href}
              locale={locale}
            >
              {primaryAction.label}
            </Link>
            {secondaryAction ? (
              <Link
                variant="button"
                to={secondaryAction.to}
                href={secondaryAction.href}
                locale={locale}
              >
                {secondaryAction.label}
              </Link>
            ) : null}
          </div>
        </div>

        {hasSupport ? (
          <aside class="homepage-hero__support">
            <p class="homepage-hero__support-text">{supportText}</p>
          </aside>
        ) : null}
      </div>
    </PageContainer>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* --- Full-bleed hero media canvas ---------------------------------------
     The <section> IS the media canvas: full page width, no contained panel,
     no border-radius. Near-viewport min-block-size (svh with a vh fallback),
     content-safe — NO max-block-size / aspect-ratio, so the hero grows when
     H1/CTA copy wraps instead of clipping the action row. display:grid makes
     the inner content cell the single in-flow grid item; align-items:end
     grounds it toward the lower/optical region. isolation:isolate contains
     the absolute children's stacking order. The page pulls this section up
     under the overlaid sticky header (--site-header-height, owned by the page). */
  .homepage-hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    display: grid;
    align-items: end;
    min-block-size: 78vh;
    min-block-size: 78svh;
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .homepage-hero {
      min-block-size: 84vh;
      min-block-size: 84svh;
    }
  }

  /* Full-bleed image: fills the entire section surface, edge to edge. object-
     cover preserves the crop without distortion. The subject is biased toward
     the right so the left copy keeps negative space (blueprint §7 — preserve
     the car as focal subject). z-index:0 anchors it beneath the overlay +
     content. */
  .homepage-hero__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 70% center;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  /* Controlled directional overlay, rebuilt for the full-width canvas. Derived
     ONLY from --color-background via color-mix (the repo scrim convention —
     ServiceCard / SiteHeader) — no raw rgba, no gold, no raw hex. Three passes:
     a left→right fade (strong behind the left copy, clears toward the right so
     the vehicle stays the focal subject), a top darken (overlaid Header chrome
     keeps AA contrast over the photograph), and a bottom settle (CTAs + support
     stay legible). Decorative (aria-hidden). */
  .homepage-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background:
      linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 6%) 0%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 30%) 45%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 58%) 100%
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 12%) 0%,
        transparent 24%,
        transparent 68%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 14%) 100%
      );
  }

  /* Inner content shell (PageContainer root): container-aligned copy grid. As
     the single in-flow grid item it is grounded to the bottom by the section's
     align-items:end. block padding is generous so the <Link> focus ring is
     never clipped and the CTAs do not pin to the extreme bottom edge. */
  .homepage-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem) clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  /* Content grid: single column by default; 7fr/5fr split (left copy / right
     support statement) at xl only (03 §Desktop content grid — the approved
     Homepage content relationship, blueprint §7 / wireframe). This is
     CONTENT-PLACEMENT only — the image fills the whole canvas behind, there is
     no separate image column (blueprint §7 / blueprint-to-ui §18). */
  .homepage-hero__content {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: end;
  }
  .homepage-hero__copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    max-inline-size: 38rem;
  }

  /* H1: semantic h1 role, active Theme V2 heading font (--font-heading —
     Inter Tight, a variable face with the full weight range). Explicit
     --font-weight-regular (400) overrides the UA bold default — the hero
     title stays a controlled regular, not heavy/bold (task §8 — avoid
     newspaper ultra-light and marketing extra-bold extremes). Left-aligned,
     tight leading, heading tracking, primary cream. max-inline-size keeps it
     ~2–3 controlled lines (blueprint §7 — ideally ~2 desktop lines); never
     display-scale, never theatrical (task §6).

     RESPONSIVE SIZING (task 1C): a component-local clamp references semantic
     type tokens — floor --text-h2, slope 5vw, cap --text-h1 — so the H1 grows
     smoothly with the viewport WITHOUT touching the global --text-h1 token
     (global tokens stay untouched). At 1440 it is strong (≈4.5rem); at
     1024–1280 laptop it is noticeably smaller (≈3.2–4rem) so it does not wrap
     into a 5-line oversized wall; at mobile it is controlled (floor --text-h2
     ≈2rem). The global --text-h1 stays the cap, so the display max is never
     reached (task §6). */
  .homepage-hero__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-regular);
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-h2), 5vw, var(--text-h1));
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    max-inline-size: 20ch;
  }

  /* Lede: Manrope, --text-lg, primary cream, controlled measure (≈31rem). */
  .homepage-hero__desc {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 31rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* CTA group: primary (platinum <Link variant="cta">) + secondary (outlined
     <Link variant="button">). The foundation <Link> owns its own
     accent/hover/focus/44px-target/prefetch treatment — no hero-specific
     button variant, no local .cta classes (03 §Colors / task §8). May wrap or
     stack on narrow widths. */
  .homepage-hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Right-side support statement (blueprint §7 / 03 §Desktop): small,
     restrained, operational, calm — a quiet muted text block with a subtle
     divider, not cards/stats/badges/icons. Bottom-aligned toward the
     lower-right region; max measure ≈28rem. The divider switches from
     block-start (mobile) to inline-start (desktop) below. */
  .homepage-hero__support {
    align-self: end;
    max-inline-size: 28rem;
  }
  .homepage-hero__support-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* ── Below xl (<80rem): single column, content-driven height. The support
     statement follows below the CTA group in DOM order; the divider becomes a
     block-start rule. (task 1D — laptop stays a single column, so the copy
     keeps the full canvas width instead of a cramped two-column text.) */
  @media (max-width: 79.99rem) {
    .homepage-hero__support {
      border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
      padding-block-start: var(--space-5);
    }
  }

  /* ── xl (>=80rem): 7/5 content split. The split activates at xl (1280px)
     rather than lg so laptop (1024–1279px) stays a comfortable full-width
     single column instead of cramped two-column text (task 1D). Panel height
     is content-safe: a near-viewport min-block-size floor and NO restrictive
     max-block-size / aspect-ratio — when the H1 wraps to more lines the hero
     GROWS to fit content instead of clipping the CTA row (task 1B). */
  @media (min-width: 80rem) {
    .homepage-hero__content--split {
      grid-template-columns: 7fr 5fr;
      gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    }
    .homepage-hero__support {
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
      border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
    }
  }
</style>
